  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=6{t}^{2}+8,$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=15$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (6{t}^{2}+8)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+8t+C \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}+8t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(1)=15.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15 & =2(1)^{3}+8(1)+C \\\\ 15 & =2+8+C \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=2{t}^{3}+8t+5.\n$$",
